@AUTHOR Björn Hagström
@WORDWRAP
@NODE MAIN "Emblem"

@{b}Emblem 1.0@{ub} - icons with default images and emblems

Emblem lets an icon borrow a shared default image (a drawer, a page) and
put an emblem on it: a small picture that says what is inside, like a
note for music or a globe for internet things. The emblem can get a soft
shadow, a glow, or be grayed, darkened or brightened.

It is an icon module for icon.library: icons in the Emblem format are put
together when they are loaded, so Workbench, file managers and every
other program that uses icon.library show them. Change one image in
ENVARC:sys/emblem and every icon that uses it changes with it.

  @{" Installing         " link INSTALL}
  @{" Quick start        " link QUICK}
  @{" The tool types     " link TOOLTYPES}
  @{" Methods (effects)  " link METHODS}
  @{" Settings file      " link PREFS}
  @{" Images and emblems " link IMAGES}
  @{" EmblemIcon command " link EMBLEMICON}
  @{" The examples       " link EXAMPLES}
  @{" Good to know       " link NOTES}
  @{" Removing Emblem    " link REMOVE}
  @{" For programmers    " link PROGRAMMERS}
  @{" History            " link HISTORY}
